<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="intro-to-linear-models">
  <title>Introduction to Linear Models</title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter introduces linear models. For the main case studies, see <xref ref="sec-regression"/>,
      <xref ref="sec-treatment-effect-models"/>, <xref ref="sec-association-tests"/>, and
      <xref ref="sec-multivariable-regression"/>. For a reminder that association is not causation, see Tyler
      Vigen's <fn><url href="https://www.tylervigen.com/spurious-correlations">Spurious Correlations</url></fn>.
    </p>
  </introduction>

</chapter>
